From bc883e9de35f4f20a8f600be58522551dffdcebd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abtraore <abdrahtraore97@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 22:47:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] kv-cache: scale the n_kv graph-reuse pad with the ubatch
 size

A 512-token prefill chunk crosses the fixed 256-token n_kv pad boundary
every chunk, so the graph was rebuilt for every chunk of a long prefill.
Padding to ~16 ubatches keeps every n_kv-derived shape stable across a
bucket of chunks: measured graphs reused 0 -> 166/166 prefill chunks on
GLM-5.3-Flash (86K prompt, 4x RTX 5090). LLAMA_PREFILL_KV_PAD_MULT
overrides (0 restores 256). Decode ubatches stay on the 256 pad.

Honest ledger: prefill throughput did NOT improve (773-795 vs a 773-935
cross-boot spread) - per-chunk graph build is milliseconds against a
~600 ms chunk, so eliminating it is noise at this ubatch size. Kept for
the reuse property itself (CPU headroom, and it makes ubatch-size sweeps
cheaper). Profiling instead points at the indexer top-k: one CUB
DeviceSegmentedSort launch per query row per MLA layer (~5.6K launches
per 512-token chunk at depth), main thread spinning in pageable-memory
DtoH copies - the batched radix-select approach (one block per row, one
launch per layer) is the remaining lever.
---
 src/llama-kv-cache.cpp | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
index ba91292..4d8a55c 100644
--- a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
@@ -1237,7 +1237,28 @@ uint32_t llama_kv_cache::get_n_kv(const slot_info & sinfo) const {
 
     // pad the n_kv value so that the graph remains constant across batches and can be reused
     // note: this also helps some backends with performance (f.ex https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/16812#issuecomment-3455112220)
-    const uint32_t n_pad_cur = std::max(n_pad, 256u);
+    //
+    // scale the pad with the ubatch size: a 512-token prefill chunk crosses a
+    // 256-token pad boundary every chunk, so the graph was rebuilt (and the
+    // whole backend-sched pass rerun) for every chunk of a long prefill -
+    // measured as the dominant, single-threaded share of deep-prefill wall
+    // time. padding to ~16 ubatches keeps every n_kv-derived shape stable
+    // across a bucket of consecutive chunks, so graph reuse engages during
+    // prefill too. decode ubatches are small, so decode keeps the 256 pad.
+    // the pad only ever widens the masked region: n_kv stays bounded by the
+    // cache size below, and empty cells are already masked by every fill.
+    // LLAMA_PREFILL_KV_PAD_MULT overrides the multiplier (0 restores 256).
+    static const uint32_t pad_mult = [] {
+        const char * env = getenv("LLAMA_PREFILL_KV_PAD_MULT");
+        return env ? (uint32_t) std::max(0, atoi(env)) : 16u;
+    }();
+
+    uint32_t n_tokens_max = 0;
+    for (uint32_t s = 0; s < sinfo.n_stream(); ++s) {
+        n_tokens_max = std::max(n_tokens_max, (uint32_t) sinfo.idxs[s].size());
+    }
+
+    const uint32_t n_pad_cur = std::max({n_pad, 256u, pad_mult*n_tokens_max});
 
     for (uint32_t s = 0; s < sinfo.n_stream(); ++s) {
         const auto & cells = v_cells[sinfo.strm[s]];
